about='''<section class="block white" id="about"><div class="wrap"><div class="section-head"><div><p class="eyebrow">02 / Experience, not a borrowed persona</p><h2>A founder's perspective.<br>A product builder's discipline.</h2></div><p>My work connects category definition and flagship-product development with the operating system underneath: instrumentation, economics, lifecycle, global distribution and organization.</p></div><div class="grid2"><div class="timeline"><article><h3>Product & engineering foundations</h3><p>Software-engineering and product-development background; earlier work across Microsoft and Tencent connects commercial intent with product requirements.</p></article><article><h3>Zynga / social-game operations</h3><p>Product Manager / Lead Producer experience across CityVille, FarmVille and Arcade products. DAU and revenue modeling, viral growth, research and experimentation.</p></article><article><h3>Gameloft / global portfolio work</h3><p>Operating experience across titles including Order & Chaos, Minion Rush and Thor 2; coordination with international studios and cross-functional teams.</p></article><article><h3>Founder / GGC / OpsGo</h3><p>Development and publishing business-building, teams, channels and launch operations. Today: game operating partnerships, incubation, research and AI-enabled workflows.</p></article></div><div><article class="card"><p class="eyebrow">Scoped historical example*</p><div class="stat">+7 percentage points</div><h3>Reported D1 retention improvement</h3><p>The Chinese CityVille project record reports +700 basis points. It is a specific historical example, not a forecast or a result attributed to every title.</p></article><article class="card rule"><p class="eyebrow">Collaboration scale*</p><div class="stat">10+ studios / 500+</div><h3>Cross-functional contributors</h3><p>International coordination experience. The contributor figure describes a collaboration network, not direct reports.</p></article><p class="small rule">*Career and project details are first-party professional records supplied by Joyce, not an independent audit. Employer/product names describe experience, not endorsements. Aggregate profit and mixed ranking claims are withheld pending scope reconciliation.</p><p class="small"><a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/minyajing/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">LinkedIn ↗</a> · <a href="https://ebooks.cmpbook.com/detail?id=26372" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Book publisher ↗</a> · <a href="../positioning/JOYCE_PERSONA.md">Evidence notes ↗</a></p></div></div></div></section>'''
sectors=[('01','Social Casino / Casino+','Player lifecycle, core/meta fit, LiveOps and monetization. Social-game scope; regulated gaming needs specialists.'),('02','Arcade / Casual','Accessible play, scalable content, retention and a commercially sound growth system.'),('03','Simulation','Progression, identity, collection, narrative and the operating cadence behind long-lived worlds.'),('04','AI-native Body, Mind & Spirit','Human-centered consumer experiences: reflection, companionship, creativity and well-being. No clinical treatment claims.')]
sector_html='<section class="block" id="sectors"><div class="wrap"><div class="section-head"><div><p class="eyebrow">03 / Four focus tracks</p><h2>Games that engage.<br>Experiences that matter.</h2></div><p>Game business is the core. AI-native body, mind and spirit products are an adjacent current-build and research track, not a claim of clinical expertise. Web3 product advisory is separately scoped.</p></div><div class="grid4">'+''.join(f'<article class="card sector"><div class="symbol">{n} /</div><h3>{e(t)}</h3><p>{e(d)}</p></article>' for n,t,d in sectors)+'</div></div></section>'
