visual='''# Joyce / GGC — Visual System v2

Date: 2026-09-19. Direction: **Lucid Systems / Warm Intelligence**.

## Identity and photography

Use Joyce's supplied real GGC-shirt portrait. Preserve face, bone structure, expression, body and clothing; only resize/compress for web. No substitute AI face, luxury persona, fabricated client scene or changed outfit. Published derivative contains no original EXIF location data.

The gold Joyce wordmark is a decorative signature-style element extracted from the supplied visual reference, not an authenticated legal signature. Use a text GGC wordmark and preserve the existing browser favicon; do not invent an official seal.

## Art direction

Clean white/lavender, clear architectural grid, restrained gold orbital lines, cobalt from the real portrait, a small hot-pink accent. System map, connected domains and subtle motion communicate future-facing capability. Human warmth comes from real photography, lively copy and playful detail; not cartoon clutter or generic luxury props.

Tokens: ink #242040; muted #666278; background #faf9ff; lavender #eee8fc; purple #6a40d9; gold #aa8440; pink #e9449e.

## Typography and interaction

Sans-serif primary type; large decisive headings; readable body copy; no microtype decorative paragraphs. Accessible focus states, horizontal table scrolling only, meaningful buttons and reduced-motion support. Decorative map/orbit graphics are not operating data. No fake live KPI dashboard.

## Source-of-truth controls

HTML typography generates the price poster from rate-card.csv. The image model's old prices, mixed service labels and percentage fees are not approved pricing authority. The live page is English; full CSV retains Chinese/English service descriptions. No service capability should be implied from a decorative image.

## Deliverables

- Real-photo English website and responsive layout.
- Six-domain interactive operating map.
- 14 capability domains, 12 anonymized service scenarios, 16 fees.
- Signed rate-card HTML; browser-rendered PNG and PDF.
- Desktop/mobile release screenshots and machine-readable QA.

Photographic derivative, wordmark and release renders are media assets. Source photo and rejected concept images are not all copied into the public repository; only release-safe assets are published.
'''
